#~ claim in the release notes does: this text is read by people deciding whether
#~ to put a mail server on the Internet. Nothing is promised that the server does
#~ not do by default or cannot be told to do.
#~
#~ It says what the package is: Progressive Robot's fork of hMailServer, not the
#~ original, which is Martin Knafve's and is developed separately, and of which
#~ packages exist - winget's hMailServer.hMailServer among them once its submission
#~ is merged. So the package name names the fork, and the moniker is the fork's
#~ (the Chocolatey id's), not "hmailserver", which a user would take for the
#~ original's (build/make-package-manifests.ps1 and
#~ build/check-package-manifests.py hold them to it).
# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://aka.ms/winget-manifest.defaultLocale.1.10.0.schema.json

