ShortDescription: Progressive Robot's fork of hMailServer, not the original - a free, open-source mail server for Windows with SMTP, IMAP and POP3, anti-spam and anti-virus filtering, DKIM, DMARC, MTA-STS, a webmail client and a REST API.
Description: |-
  This is Progressive Robot's fork of hMailServer, not the original. The original hMailServer
  is Martin Knafve's; it is developed separately and has releases of its own, and packages of
  it exist. Progressive Robot Ltd forked it in 2026 and released 6.0.0, the fork's first
  release, on 12 June 2026.

  hMailServer is a free, open-source mail server implementing SMTP, IMAP and POP3, with a
  Windows administration program, a browser administration console, a webmail client and a
  REST API. The fork brings a current toolchain, current cryptography, and current
  transport-security and authentication standards, and upgrades an installation of the
  original up to 5.6 in place, with a continuous database upgrade chain from each of its
  versions. It does not upgrade the original's 5.7 releases of September 2026: its database
  upgrade has no step from their database versions, 5709 and 5711. Both installers register
  under the same uninstall entry, hMailServer_is1, so on a machine where the original is
  installed this package's installer takes that installation for its own; do not install it
  over the original's 5.7. The database upgrade is one-way: take a backup first.

  What it does: SMTP with submission and implicit TLS, IMAP4rev1 with the extensions a
  modern client asks for, POP3, ManageSieve, SPF, DKIM signing and verification, DMARC with
  reporting, MTA-STS and TLS-RPT, DANE, ARC, SpamAssassin and ClamAV integration, greylisting,
  DNS blacklists and SURBL, auto-ban, two-factor authentication for administrators and
  accounts, application passwords, OAuth 2.0 (inbound and outbound, including Microsoft 365),
  CardDAV address books, full-text search, quarantine, archiving and legal holds, backup and
  restore, Prometheus metrics and OpenTelemetry export.

  Every release is validated by the full regression suite run against the exact binary that
  ships, with live SpamAssassin and ClamAV, and SPF, DKIM and DMARC evaluated through the
  resolver code path - nothing but DNS is mocked. The installer is Authenticode-signed, and
  every release the project's CI signs carries an SBOM and Sigstore signatures.

  This package installs the server, the Control Panel and the setup tools. An unattended
  install configures the embedded database and leaves the administrator password unset:
  set one from the Control Panel before the server is reachable from anywhere but the
  machine itself.
Moniker: hmailserver-progressiverobot
